1
00:00:08,660 --> 00:00:13,340
Try letting peace go lightly,
and step away from it.

2
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:26,880
aiming for the sunset
floating over the Nakagawa.

3
00:00:27,900 --> 00:00:33,980
Kick a pebble and even
your shoe goes flying.

4
00:00:33,980 --> 00:00:42,280
onto the head of the carpenter
who had been saving his money,

5
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:48,440
they laugh that you're still just a kid.

6
00:00:49,220 --> 00:00:53,560
Even if you somehow rouse
your energy somewhere,

7
00:00:53,560 --> 00:00:58,620
Katsushika Kameari,
not even one yawn changes.

8
00:00:58,620 --> 00:01:02,500
the streetscape feels strangely gentle.

9
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:10,460
From the pointed hat, from the water basin,

10
00:01:11,180 --> 00:01:16,800
the sunset falls toward the big shop.

11
00:01:20,930 --> 00:01:25,260
Why does tomorrow end too,

12
00:01:25,260 --> 00:01:30,400
Katsushika Shibamata,
even happiness is lost,

13
00:01:32,400 --> 00:01:34,420
because I've been left alone,

14
00:01:38,540 --> 00:01:40,960
the turtle's repayment of kindness.

15
00:01:43,940 --> 00:01:45,720
Bullying the turtle.

16
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:49,440
Turtle, turtle, turtle,
turtle, turtle, turtle.

17
00:01:49,440 --> 00:01:52,940
Hey, hey, hey, hey, hey, kids!

18
00:01:52,940 --> 00:01:54,260
What is it, mister?

19
00:01:54,260 --> 00:01:59,200
You mustn't bully the turtle.

20
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:01,340
No, no, stop!

21
00:02:02,400 --> 00:02:08,240
I'm not saying it was bad, it was quite a good performance,
I think, but whenever you two are together,

22
00:02:08,240 --> 00:02:13,860
it's hot-headed. Ryotsu's the one who assigned the roles,
but so am I.

23
00:02:14,240 --> 00:02:17,480
Honestly, I really don't want to
play the kid who bullies the turtle.

24
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:22,120
I only reluctantly agreed because it's a play for the kids' club,
you know.

25
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:29,940
Ryo-san, the Chief told you there'd be no bonus unless you get serious, right?
So be serious.

26
00:02:29,940 --> 00:02:30,820
What do you think you're doing?

27
00:02:30,820 --> 00:02:32,520
Besides, it's too long.

28
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:34,940
The worst one here is you.

29
00:02:34,940 --> 00:02:36,720
M-me?

30
00:02:37,260 --> 00:02:41,100
Do you even know what kind
of person Urashima Taro was?

31
00:02:41,880 --> 00:02:43,600
He was a fisherman, right?

32
00:02:43,600 --> 00:02:44,080
That's right.

33
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:48,520
Day after day, he went out to sea
and made his living catching fish.

34
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:50,640
Listen, when you go out to sea,

35
00:02:51,200 --> 00:02:52,520
it's not always sunny days.

36
00:02:53,260 --> 00:02:54,640
There were rainy days, too.

37
00:02:55,220 --> 00:02:56,920
There were snowy days, too.

38
00:02:57,320 --> 00:02:58,840
He went out fishing on stormy days,

39
00:02:59,940 --> 00:03:01,920
and there may have been
times he got swept away.

40
00:03:03,820 --> 00:03:07,320
And on top of that, he's the kind of softhearted
fool who helps a turtle that's being bullied.

41
00:03:07,320 --> 00:03:09,700
There's no way he lives a wealthy life.

42
00:03:10,080 --> 00:03:13,920
He must have kept wearing the same
outfit until it was in tatters.

43
00:03:14,380 --> 00:03:17,500
The torn parts were mended with
needles made from fish bones

44
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:20,920
and thread made from
dried jellyfish intestines.

45
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:25,380
Do you really think a man like that has such fresh,
white skin?

46
00:03:26,080 --> 00:03:29,360
Do you think he has hair
neatly styled like this?

47
00:03:29,940 --> 00:03:33,700
Do you really think he'd wear
clothes fresh from the dry cleaner's?

48
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:39,880
Your appearance right now shows no
trace of the harshness of life at sea.

49
00:03:39,880 --> 00:03:43,000
It's completely lacking in realism.

50
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:45,880
Y-yeah, now that you mention it...

51
00:03:45,880 --> 00:03:51,180
But for Takada to stress realism
that much in a children's play...

52
00:03:51,180 --> 00:03:55,820
Idiot! Kids these days have a much
sharper eye than the adults around here!

53
00:03:56,240 --> 00:03:58,940
If they sense even the
slightest corner-cutting...

54
00:04:00,060 --> 00:04:01,680
It's close, you know.

55
00:04:01,680 --> 00:04:05,360
And what about my bonus if that happens?

56
00:04:05,360 --> 00:04:10,000
You've still got 30 years left on your house loan too,
don't you?

57
00:04:10,660 --> 00:04:11,620
Sorry.

58
00:04:12,340 --> 00:04:13,660
Hey, Ryo-chan.

59
00:04:13,660 --> 00:04:18,740
When's Otohime's entrance?

60
00:04:18,740 --> 00:04:22,100
She looks just like the real Otohime.

61
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:24,440
Reiko, that really suits you.

62
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:25,260
Really?

63
00:04:25,260 --> 00:04:27,220
It's not right at all.

64
00:04:27,900 --> 00:04:30,520
What's wrong with this outfit?

65
00:04:30,520 --> 00:04:31,760
Everything.

66
00:04:31,760 --> 00:04:36,320
Reiko, how many years do you think
Urashima Taro spent in the Dragon Palace?

67
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:37,260
That's...

68
00:04:38,100 --> 00:04:40,760
When Urashima Taro returned to his village,

69
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:43,480
no one he knew was left there anymore.

70
00:04:44,040 --> 00:04:49,380
And when he opened the tamatebako,
Urashima turned into a white-haired old man.

71
00:04:50,220 --> 00:04:52,580
Considering the life expectancy back then,

72
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:53,960
fifty years.

73
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:58,360
That means he must have stayed in the
Dragon Palace for at least fifty years.

74
00:04:58,360 --> 00:04:59,100
I see.

75
00:04:59,660 --> 00:05:05,500
Do you really think you can keep Urashima Taro in
the Dragon Palace for fifty years dressed like that?

76
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:07,840
Then he'd stay three days at most.

77
00:05:07,840 --> 00:05:10,500
Then what kind of outfit would work?

78
00:05:10,500 --> 00:05:12,220
Well, that's...

79
00:05:14,320 --> 00:05:15,640
Hey, what are you doing?

80
00:05:15,640 --> 00:05:20,520
In other words, she has to be that
alluring to keep a man from leaving.

81
00:05:20,520 --> 00:05:22,900
It's a matter of realism.

82
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:26,220
Then what about Ryo-chan playing the turtle?

83
00:05:26,220 --> 00:05:28,820
You're going to dress as
a realistic turtle, right?

84
00:05:31,140 --> 00:05:32,420
Leave it to me.

85
00:05:50,520 --> 00:05:50,800
Mm.

86
00:05:52,740 --> 00:05:53,140
Mm.

87
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:54,080
Mm.

88
00:05:54,080 --> 00:05:54,260
Mm.

89
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:01,100
Be a good boy and stay still, okay?

90
00:06:02,540 --> 00:06:04,880
I'm just going to borrow your
shoulder for a moment, got it?

91
00:06:04,880 --> 00:06:06,140
I'm staying still.

92
00:06:06,920 --> 00:06:09,200
Taking a shoulder from a real turtle!

93
00:06:09,640 --> 00:06:11,000
Just like Ryotsu, typical.

94
00:06:14,860 --> 00:06:16,680
So this is the turtle costume.

95
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:19,240
It looks so real, just like the real thing.

96
00:06:20,740 --> 00:06:23,680
Ryo-san's really focused
on realism this time, so.

97
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:25,340
My bonus is riding on this too.

98
00:06:26,040 --> 00:06:29,780
I wish you'd put this much
effort into your regular work.

99
00:06:31,880 --> 00:06:33,880
Nakagawa's Ferrari.

100
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:37,020
Nakagawa-san.

101
00:06:37,020 --> 00:06:41,320
Good morning.

102
00:06:42,320 --> 00:06:43,860
W-wait, is that Nakagawa?

103
00:06:43,860 --> 00:06:46,640
Well, I took my senior's
advice as a reference.

104
00:06:46,640 --> 00:06:49,060
I went all out pursuing realism.

105
00:06:50,520 --> 00:06:52,240
It's the ultimate Urashima Taro, right?

106
00:06:52,240 --> 00:06:54,140
It's certainly realistic, but...

107
00:06:54,140 --> 00:06:56,040
Nakagawa-san's image is...

108
00:06:56,040 --> 00:06:58,240
It's all Ryotsu's fault.

109
00:07:03,460 --> 00:07:04,180
W-what is this...

110
00:07:04,180 --> 00:07:05,780
Reiko-san,

111
00:07:09,200 --> 00:07:09,622
how do I look?

112
00:07:09,672 --> 00:07:11,514
Ryo-chan kept nagging me,

113
00:07:11,564 --> 00:07:14,520
so I went all out with a bold,
realistic Otohime.

114
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:17,225
S-sure, it's realistic, but...

115
00:07:17,275 --> 00:07:19,120
you didn't have to go that far...

116
00:07:19,120 --> 00:07:21,620
Reiko-san, you're totally off character.

117
00:07:21,900 --> 00:07:23,520
Ahaha, really?

118
00:07:23,640 --> 00:07:26,340
Making Reiko wear something like this!

119
00:07:27,020 --> 00:07:29,460
That caveman, I'll never forgive him!

120
00:07:30,300 --> 00:07:32,820
By the way, where's Ryotsu, the key person?

121
00:07:33,320 --> 00:07:35,380
Today's the real children's club performance,
you know.

122
00:07:36,040 --> 00:07:37,580
He's already here.

123
00:07:42,320 --> 00:07:44,220
Who did you say you won't forgive?

124
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:49,200
It's me, right here, Chief!

125
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:52,900
They can pull their limbs inside it?!

126
00:07:52,900 --> 00:07:55,520
It's realistic, so just...

127
00:08:09,380 --> 00:08:13,287
Because I made it so realistic,
it's over 50 kilos in weight,

128
00:08:13,337 --> 00:08:15,620
and it's so exhausting just to stand up.

129
00:08:15,860 --> 00:08:16,760
That's rough.

130
00:08:17,300 --> 00:08:18,640
That thing from earlier was weird!

131
00:08:18,780 --> 00:08:21,520
Stop! Turtles tip over easily!

132
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:25,880
Damn it, I can't reach.

133
00:08:26,320 --> 00:08:28,280
If I've got to, I'll use the momentum...

134
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:32,130
1, 2, 1,

135
00:08:32,180 --> 00:08:34,600
1, 2, 3!

136
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:40,100
So close!

137
00:08:40,400 --> 00:08:42,100
You were so close, senpai!

138
00:08:42,380 --> 00:08:44,200
Alright, one more try!

139
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:44,720
Okay!

140
00:08:45,200 --> 00:08:45,900
Whoa!

141
00:08:46,480 --> 00:08:48,740
Hey, couldn't someone just give me a hand?!

142
00:08:50,540 --> 00:08:52,960
I'm going to go practice the
turtle's movements for a bit.

143
00:08:53,580 --> 00:08:57,800
If I don't get used to this weight now,
I'll be in trouble during the actual show.

144
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:00,440
You know what time the play starts, right?

145
00:09:00,760 --> 00:09:02,540
If you're late, there's no bonus!

146
00:09:02,920 --> 00:09:04,200
I know.

147
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:12,500
Looks like we can practice
to our heart's content here.

148
00:09:14,580 --> 00:09:17,020
Suddenly I've got the urge.

149
00:09:17,660 --> 00:09:19,420
I've no choice, right here.

150
00:09:20,840 --> 00:09:22,000
Is it a bit...?

151
00:09:22,860 --> 00:09:24,200
You bastard, this...

152
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:27,780
My shoulder's dislocated.

153
00:09:27,780 --> 00:09:29,720
Ow

154
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:32,660
This shell, you'll be unable to get up!

155
00:09:35,440 --> 00:09:36,120
A dog's...

156
00:09:41,860 --> 00:09:43,100
Whoa, left, right!

157
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:48,320
What should we do?
Let's go back to the police box for now.

158
00:09:50,980 --> 00:09:51,800
Whoa!

159
00:09:52,500 --> 00:09:56,340
Over here, apparently it's the river.

160
00:10:06,880 --> 00:10:07,840
Oh no

161
00:10:13,980 --> 00:10:15,080
Phew, that was close

162
00:10:15,080 --> 00:10:18,160
If I die looking like this,
it'll be a disgrace all the way to Matsudai!

163
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:19,000
What was that just now?

164
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:20,600
Not good

165
00:10:20,600 --> 00:10:23,280
Something huge just leapt out of the river!

166
00:10:23,280 --> 00:10:23,820
Really?

167
00:10:23,820 --> 00:10:24,560
This way, this way!

168
00:10:24,560 --> 00:10:25,760
It's coming this way!

169
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:26,900
It's a turtle!

170
00:10:26,900 --> 00:10:27,720
It's huge!

171
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:29,600
Hey, it's getting away! Wait!

172
00:10:31,820 --> 00:10:32,880
This is fun!

173
00:10:32,880 --> 00:10:34,740
Hey, you guys should try riding it too.

174
00:10:36,760 --> 00:10:38,400
Knock it off already, you two.

175
00:10:39,380 --> 00:10:40,480
The turtle talked!

176
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:41,820
It's a human-faced turtle!

177
00:10:41,820 --> 00:10:45,120
Turtles aren't scary if
you just flip them over.

178
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:45,740
I see.

179
00:10:45,740 --> 00:10:46,420
Here we go!

180
00:10:47,620 --> 00:10:48,720
Stop it!

181
00:10:48,720 --> 00:10:50,960
Just because you think I'm a kid...

182
00:10:50,960 --> 00:10:54,520
Stop it, please stop!

183
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:55,740
Damn it.

184
00:10:55,740 --> 00:10:57,400
If this were a fairy tale,

185
00:10:57,400 --> 00:10:59,640
Urashima Taro would come to save me.

186
00:10:59,640 --> 00:11:02,260
Isn't there a turtle around here?

187
00:11:03,420 --> 00:11:04,380
Someone's in trouble.

188
00:11:04,380 --> 00:11:06,760
Isn't there a turtle around here?

189
00:11:07,600 --> 00:11:08,840
To the children,

190
00:11:10,380 --> 00:11:13,680
Isn't there a turtle in trouble around here?

191
00:11:25,580 --> 00:11:31,880
Isn't there a turtle who's in
trouble from being bullied by children?

192
00:11:31,880 --> 00:11:32,840
Eeeeeeh!

193
00:11:37,860 --> 00:11:43,360
Now, now, children,
you mustn't bully turtles.

194
00:11:44,440 --> 00:11:45,880
Aaaaaaah!

195
00:11:53,260 --> 00:11:54,340
Saved!

196
00:11:56,840 --> 00:11:58,340
Whoa! It's a ghost!

197
00:11:59,320 --> 00:12:01,220
Don't wander around, rest in peace!

198
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:03,440
I am Urashima Taro.

199
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:05,840
So you're Urashima Taro's ghost, right?

200
00:12:06,260 --> 00:12:07,940
I'm not dead.

201
00:12:08,420 --> 00:12:11,120
Then you opened the tamatebako
and became like that?

202
00:12:11,780 --> 00:12:13,040
You haven't opened it yet.

203
00:12:13,040 --> 00:12:15,820
Well, I did save you, so

204
00:12:15,820 --> 00:12:18,580
you'll take me to the Dragon Palace.

205
00:12:18,580 --> 00:12:19,160
Ow

206
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:21,680
Both my shoulders are dislocated,
and it hurts!

207
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:23,540
Are you hurt?

208
00:12:25,340 --> 00:12:30,740
It's not like that. You should come to my house,
but after that, you have to take me to the Dragon

209
00:12:30,740 --> 00:12:34,820
Palace, you know.

210
00:12:36,180 --> 00:12:38,300
What is this old man?

211
00:12:38,300 --> 00:13:02,360
Mmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm...

212
00:13:02,360 --> 00:13:05,100
I've left the running of things to my children,
you know.

213
00:13:05,100 --> 00:13:06,520
Click, and on to victory!

214
00:13:11,540 --> 00:13:13,240
Welcome back.

215
00:13:13,240 --> 00:13:15,700
Welcome back.

216
00:13:17,800 --> 00:13:19,640
It's like the Dragon Palace!

217
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:21,780
It's all fake, after all.

218
00:13:21,780 --> 00:13:24,280
The most important thing is missing!

219
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:26,080
The most important thing?

220
00:13:26,540 --> 00:13:28,420
In order to get that, too,

221
00:13:28,420 --> 00:13:32,100
we absolutely must get to the Dragon Palace.

222
00:13:34,200 --> 00:13:37,660
Hirame Six, is Hirame Six here?

223
00:13:39,300 --> 00:13:41,180
Come with me to my room right away.

224
00:13:41,180 --> 00:13:42,900
Very well.

225
00:13:43,840 --> 00:13:45,600
Seriously, it's Hirame?

226
00:13:46,920 --> 00:13:49,300
My room is back here.

227
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:49,980
See?

228
00:13:56,900 --> 00:14:00,700
Why is there such a shabby
shack inside the building?

229
00:14:01,120 --> 00:14:03,860
I'm Urashima Taro, after all,
so I'm not getting involved.

230
00:14:13,260 --> 00:14:14,980
It doesn't hurt at all anymore!

231
00:14:15,820 --> 00:14:16,620
Thank you, sensei.

232
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:18,380
You've done well.

233
00:14:22,980 --> 00:14:24,520
Mm, thanks for that, old man.

234
00:14:24,860 --> 00:14:25,580
I see.

235
00:14:25,660 --> 00:14:25,980
Whoa!

236
00:14:26,100 --> 00:14:29,800
Right away,
I'll take you to the Dragon Palace, turtle.

237
00:14:29,960 --> 00:14:32,380
Wait a minute, are you serious, old man?

238
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:35,825
Indeed, to octopuses and abalones alike,

239
00:14:35,875 --> 00:14:38,540
I've studied Urashima Taro for 78 years,

240
00:14:38,590 --> 00:14:42,520
I've got proof that the
Dragon Palace really exists.

241
00:14:42,700 --> 00:14:43,940
Really?

242
00:14:45,660 --> 00:14:46,340
Me.

243
00:14:47,040 --> 00:14:50,860
Something's fishy.
The Dragon Palace was in Tokyo Bay?

244
00:14:51,540 --> 00:14:54,440
If you know where it is,
just go by yourself.

245
00:14:54,440 --> 00:14:56,120
Don't drag me into this.

246
00:14:56,120 --> 00:14:59,280
At first,
I too thought that with just this map,

247
00:14:59,280 --> 00:15:01,860
I could reach the Dragon Palace.

248
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:04,505
Alright,

249
00:15:04,555 --> 00:15:13,540
We're almost at the Dragon Palace!

250
00:15:28,180 --> 00:15:29,140
It's the truth, I swear.

251
00:15:36,940 --> 00:15:37,900
This time for real.

252
00:15:48,080 --> 00:15:49,160
Sorry,

253
00:15:49,210 --> 00:15:52,320
then, this time, the truth.

254
00:15:58,700 --> 00:15:59,860
This time for real.

255
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:02,600
Enough already.

256
00:16:03,260 --> 00:16:06,520
What is it this time, a killer whale,
a dolphin, or a sea otter?

257
00:16:07,160 --> 00:16:11,580
No matter how many times I went,
I never managed to reach the Dragon Palace.

258
00:16:11,580 --> 00:16:13,440
I agonized over it.

259
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:16,480
But one day, I finally figured it out.

260
00:16:16,940 --> 00:16:22,600
Long ago, Urashima, to the turtle he saved

261
00:16:23,300 --> 00:16:25,740
So that's how it was!

262
00:16:25,740 --> 00:16:30,140
The key to reaching the
Dragon Palace was in this song!

263
00:16:31,760 --> 00:16:34,000
That is,

264
00:16:34,900 --> 00:16:38,300
one must be led by the turtle one saved

265
00:16:39,080 --> 00:16:42,140
unless one is taken there
by the turtle one saved,

266
00:16:42,140 --> 00:16:45,120
one can never reach the Dragon Palace.

267
00:16:47,300 --> 00:16:50,020
Stop spinning on people's backs!

268
00:16:51,820 --> 00:16:52,860
Sorry.

269
00:16:53,420 --> 00:16:58,200
So I immediately changed
my name to Urashima Taro,

270
00:16:58,200 --> 00:17:02,980
and from that day on,
I ran all over the country to save turtles.

271
00:17:14,240 --> 00:17:16,680
The turtles I've saved so far

272
00:17:21,120 --> 00:17:22,080
number 9,997,

273
00:17:23,220 --> 00:17:27,540
but not one of them has
taken me to the Dragon Palace.

274
00:17:27,540 --> 00:17:28,880
Well, obviously.

275
00:17:28,880 --> 00:17:33,820
You're exactly the ten-thousandth.

276
00:17:33,820 --> 00:17:37,360
Now take me to the Dragon Palace, turtle!

277
00:17:37,360 --> 00:17:38,600
Don't be ridiculous!

278
00:17:38,600 --> 00:17:41,920
I have to perform in the children's club play,
you know!

279
00:17:42,520 --> 00:17:44,400
Besides, I'm not a turtle, I'm...

280
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:45,700
Wait.

281
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:47,920
They're this rich.

282
00:17:47,920 --> 00:17:50,060
There's no harm in staying
on good terms with them.

283
00:17:50,060 --> 00:17:51,540
And that map...

284
00:17:52,860 --> 00:17:54,480
Isn't it a map showing something?

285
00:17:55,660 --> 00:17:58,520
Like, a ship that sank along with treasure?

286
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:02,140
Maybe this is a big
money-making opportunity!

287
00:18:02,820 --> 00:18:04,780
Aha! Lord Urashima Taro!

288
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:07,840
As you wish,
I'll take you to the Dragon Palace!

289
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:11,240
So you're in the mood now, turtle!

290
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:14,980
Now my wish will finally come true!

291
00:18:17,760 --> 00:18:19,020
He's late, Ryotsu.

292
00:18:19,020 --> 00:18:22,060
I've been calling his cell
phone over and over since earlier,

293
00:18:22,860 --> 00:18:23,780
but it won't go through at all.

294
00:18:24,460 --> 00:18:26,940
I shouldn't have counted on him after all.

295
00:18:27,500 --> 00:18:29,620
I guess we have no choice but to
give the turtle the important role.

296
00:18:32,800 --> 00:18:34,620
Right, straight on from here.

297
00:18:37,700 --> 00:18:38,433
Hey,

298
00:18:38,483 --> 00:18:41,880
let's take the train as far as near Ryujo.

299
00:18:47,060 --> 00:18:49,500
Good thing we had the turtle to ride on,
old woman.

300
00:18:49,500 --> 00:18:50,330
Indeed,

301
00:18:50,380 --> 00:18:54,120
at times like this,
a turtle is worth more than all those years.

302
00:18:54,120 --> 00:18:56,140
Don't talk such nonsense.

303
00:18:56,140 --> 00:18:57,053
Hey,

304
00:18:57,103 --> 00:19:01,600
you'll need an oxygen tank from here on.

305
00:19:02,280 --> 00:19:03,940
let's get it arranged right away.

306
00:19:03,940 --> 00:19:05,900
Here goes, click!

307
00:19:11,300 --> 00:19:11,900
Whoa!

308
00:19:30,820 --> 00:19:32,180
Well, let's go.

309
00:19:32,180 --> 00:19:33,540
No, as for my share,

310
00:19:33,540 --> 00:19:35,640
a mask doesn't need one, does it?

311
00:19:35,640 --> 00:19:40,840
No, if you stay on land too long,
you forget how to breathe.

312
00:19:41,820 --> 00:19:43,520
What a hopeless guy.

313
00:19:43,520 --> 00:19:45,220
Click, there we go.

314
00:19:54,700 --> 00:19:56,960
According to the map,
we should be about there by now.

315
00:19:58,000 --> 00:19:58,720
W-what is it?

316
00:20:01,540 --> 00:20:04,760
The tide currents are
getting strong around here.

317
00:20:05,180 --> 00:20:07,020
Wall or not, I know that much.

318
00:20:07,020 --> 00:20:09,980
Damn it,
I won't give up over something this small!

319
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:14,520
Do something, wall!

320
00:20:14,520 --> 00:20:17,100
You said "do something," didn't you?

321
00:20:21,040 --> 00:20:22,260
The Dragon Palace!

322
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:27,820
As expected of a turtle!

323
00:20:34,340 --> 00:20:35,620
What the heck is this?

324
00:20:37,460 --> 00:20:39,440
Isn't that a sunken battleship?

325
00:20:40,920 --> 00:20:43,380
Why would it be in a place like this?

326
00:20:44,300 --> 00:20:47,860
So the treasure's hidden in this ship

327
00:20:47,860 --> 00:20:49,920
Treasure, treasure!

328
00:20:50,720 --> 00:20:51,840
Treasure.

329
00:20:53,620 --> 00:21:03,920
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

330
00:21:03,920 --> 00:21:04,800
Aaaaaah!

331
00:21:06,540 --> 00:21:14,380
A huge box... could this be the treasure box?
Open it and get a shock, it's the Tamatebako, hahaha!

332
00:21:16,940 --> 00:21:22,140
Okay, on three we open it! One, two, three!

333
00:21:22,140 --> 00:21:24,180
Aaaaaah!

334
00:21:26,620 --> 00:21:28,080
Aaaaaah!

335
00:21:54,460 --> 00:21:56,620
Let me give you this as a souvenir.

336
00:21:57,780 --> 00:22:00,560
You should open it when
you're really in trouble.

337
00:22:00,560 --> 00:22:04,120
Yes, thank you, Princess Otohime.

338
00:22:04,120 --> 00:22:21,700
He's turned into a real old man!

339
00:22:21,860 --> 00:22:23,080
How realistic!

340
00:22:26,080 --> 00:22:27,500
Yay!

341
00:22:28,080 --> 00:22:29,240
Yay!

342
00:22:31,120 --> 00:22:34,320
Quite the opposite, I'm totally into it.

343
00:22:34,320 --> 00:22:35,080
Are you all right?

344
00:22:35,400 --> 00:22:38,380
Are you Princess Otohime?

345
00:22:38,700 --> 00:22:41,800
N-no, well I mean...

346
00:22:41,800 --> 00:22:44,449
Yes! I've finally found her.

347
00:22:44,499 --> 00:22:46,620
Now I have no regrets in life.

348
00:22:47,520 --> 00:22:48,434
I'm...

349
00:22:48,484 --> 00:22:51,860
I'm going to make Princess Otohime mine!

350
00:22:52,200 --> 00:22:53,260
Let go of me!

351
00:22:54,260 --> 00:22:56,020
It's really good, isn't it!

352
00:22:57,060 --> 00:22:57,840
Yay!

353
00:22:59,760 --> 00:23:00,200
Good!

354
00:23:06,180 --> 00:23:08,080
So?

355
00:23:08,520 --> 00:23:10,566
According to my detailed research,

356
00:23:10,616 --> 00:23:14,060
there have been many maritime accidents
around that area since long ago.

357
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:17,900
I heard a destroyer sank
during exercises recently, too.

358
00:23:19,040 --> 00:23:24,000
Then why did that old man's map
have the Dragon Palace written on it?

359
00:23:24,640 --> 00:23:28,000
Apparently,
a person who nearly got lost there long ago

360
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:31,520
turned white-haired
overnight from sheer terror,

361
00:23:31,960 --> 00:23:33,580
and that's why it was called that.

362
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:35,900
Oh my God.

363
00:23:40,260 --> 00:23:41,540
Hey, cut it out.

364
00:23:42,560 --> 00:23:46,880
Put that outfit on again and get
angry like some Princess Otohime!

365
00:23:48,280 --> 00:23:50,220
It was my dream!

366
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:52,740
Jarome, once more!

367
00:23:53,600 --> 00:23:56,000
If I say no, then no!

368
00:24:15,000 --> 00:24:23,280
Surprise and commotion,
with spirit and resolution, swiftly erased

369
00:24:23,720 --> 00:24:34,960
decided, with inspiration and bounce,
wrapped up, action, and flying away

370
00:24:35,900 --> 00:24:40,080
Above all, the amazing power

371
00:24:40,080 --> 00:24:51,980
Everyone gather, come here,
the dreamlike final energy

372
00:24:53,000 --> 00:25:03,000
Gazing at tomorrow, believing in yesterday, drawing the universe,
standing on the ground, the star of Kameari comes

373
00:25:05,120 --> 00:25:08,200
"Is this good enough?"
"As if it's good enough!"

374
00:25:32,960 --> 00:25:36,160
Next time: The Chief's transformed new car

375
00:25:36,160 --> 00:25:37,240
See you

376
00:25:41,960 --> 00:25:43,360
Thank you for watching.

